<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communist Party of Nepal (Maoist Centre)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1994">1994</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CPN (Maoist Centre), Communist Party of Nepal (Maoist), CPN (Maoist)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-unified-marxist-leninist">Communist Party of Nepal</a> (Maoist Centre) is a Nepalese party led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pushpa-kamal-dahal">Pushpa Kamal Dahal</a> (Prachanda). As the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> (Maoist) it waged an armed insurgency, the People's War, from 1996 to 2006, in which some 17,000 people died. After the peace agreement of 2006 it entered politics, won the most seats in the 2008 Constituent Assembly that abolished the monarchy, and took its present name in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-maoist-centre.jpg" alt="Communist Party of Nepal (Maoist Centre)" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Communist Party of Nepal (Maoist Centre) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Nepal_(Maoist_Centre).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
